# Portal configuration. Copy to .env.local and fill in; .env*.local is gitignored.
#
# NOTHING HERE IS A VALUE, DELIBERATELY. This file names what must be set and
# says what each one is for. Real keys live in the environment and, for an
# operator, in the sync service's RUNBOOK.md - never in a repository.

# The Supabase project URL. Also used by next.config.js to derive the storage
# host for next/image, so an unset value makes remote images refuse rather than
# silently half-load.
SUPABASE_URL=

# The ANON key. This is what a signed-in student's own session is built on, so
# migration 0053's row security decides what it can read. Public by design - it
# is safe in a browser - but it is server-side here because the whole auth flow
# runs through route handlers, which keeps it out of the client bundle too.
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# The SERVICE ROLE key. It BYPASSES ROW SECURITY ENTIRELY and must never reach
# the browser: no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, and nothing importing app/lib/supabase.ts
# may be a client component.
#
# The dashboard no longer needs it - /students/me reads through the viewer's own
# session. What still does is app/api/v1/uploads, which takes a studentId from
# the caller and asks nobody who they are. That route is the remaining hole.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
